WEBVTT

00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:22.980
Now, then.

00:00:27.650 --> 00:00:28.480
Yes.

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:31.900
The lecture will be ending soon.

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:36.910
We will head over there
once the meet and greet is over.

00:00:42.330 --> 00:00:43.710
Yes, I understand.

00:00:48.290 --> 00:00:49.750
I will let her know as well.

00:01:03.560 --> 00:01:04.390
Can I help you?

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:08.610
I'd like a meeting with
Ms. Anna Winehouse.

00:01:09.730 --> 00:01:11.820
Do you have an appointment, sir?

00:01:12.530 --> 00:01:14.030
No, but it's urgent.

00:01:17.660 --> 00:01:21.290
Then please go through
the proper channels.

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:25.870
One of her friends was involved
in an incident.

00:01:26.420 --> 00:01:28.460
Something that may put her in danger.

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:36.680
I'm James Blood with the SSC.

00:01:44.220 --> 00:01:46.600
My apologies, I did not realize
you were a policeman.

00:01:48.350 --> 00:01:50.310
I'm her personal assistant, Jasper.

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:52.900
What incident are you referring to?

00:01:54.530 --> 00:01:55.650
It's rather sensitive.

00:01:57.820 --> 00:01:59.910
I'd like to talk to her directly.

00:02:05.870 --> 00:02:08.040
Understood. Please wait here.

00:02:08.790 --> 00:02:10.420
<i>That was a wonderful speech.</i>

00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:12.750
The pharmaceutical industry
has a bright future.

00:02:13.380 --> 00:02:14.420
Thank you.

00:02:23.180 --> 00:02:25.520
Now, regarding our joint venture...

00:04:22.550 --> 00:04:23.510
Would you like one?

00:04:37.690 --> 00:04:40.530
Vitamin deficiency affects
our ability to think.

00:04:41.230 --> 00:04:43.400
No, thank you. I won't be long.

00:04:56.420 --> 00:04:57.920
I'm Anna Winehouse.

00:05:00.050 --> 00:05:02.510
I'm James Blood with the SSC.

00:05:03.720 --> 00:05:05.050
I heard from Jasper.

00:05:06.340 --> 00:05:08.970
It doesn't seem you came
to hear my speech.

00:05:10.310 --> 00:05:11.140
My apologies.

00:05:13.520 --> 00:05:15.350
What can I do for you,

00:05:16.350 --> 00:05:18.230
Detective James Blood?

00:05:29.410 --> 00:05:31.030
I believe that you are familiar

00:05:31.700 --> 00:05:32.700
with this man.

00:05:35.330 --> 00:05:39.250
There isn't anyone in the scientific field
who wouldn't be.

00:05:41.550 --> 00:05:42.960
Fred Faraday.

00:05:44.920 --> 00:05:46.340
He is a man at the forefront

00:05:46.970 --> 00:05:49.640
of biochemistry,
particularly in the field...

00:05:50.930 --> 00:05:52.930
of genetic engineering.

00:06:06.780 --> 00:06:09.530
His vehicle was discovered
at the bottom of a river.

00:06:13.870 --> 00:06:15.700
Does that mean he's dead?

00:06:17.210 --> 00:06:19.080
A body has not been found yet.

00:06:29.180 --> 00:06:30.720
Why did you come to me?

00:06:36.390 --> 00:06:40.770
We found a number of photographs
of you two together at his residence.

00:06:46.860 --> 00:06:49.200
It seems you are quite close to him.

00:06:53.070 --> 00:06:56.290
What are you looking to learn from me,
Detective?

00:06:57.500 --> 00:06:58.870
I have no ulterior motive.

00:07:00.870 --> 00:07:05.840
Do you know what he was researching last?

00:07:08.590 --> 00:07:09.630
Researching?

00:07:14.850 --> 00:07:16.720
Are you saying that it is connected

00:07:17.560 --> 00:07:19.020
to his whereabouts?

00:07:30.780 --> 00:07:32.950
Files or documents on LIVE...

00:07:37.240 --> 00:07:40.160
There was none of that from Monica's room.

00:07:44.790 --> 00:07:47.300
The only clues Monica left...

00:07:50.170 --> 00:07:51.840
were hidden.

00:08:12.240 --> 00:08:13.070
Hey!

00:08:14.030 --> 00:08:14.910
Bad kitty!

00:08:17.660 --> 00:08:20.080
Eat that at your bowl!

00:08:23.290 --> 00:08:24.120
Honestly,

00:08:24.750 --> 00:08:26.170
nobody's going to steal--

00:08:28.380 --> 00:08:29.210
<i>Steal?</i>

00:08:29.750 --> 00:08:30.590
<i>Was that it?</i>

00:08:31.210 --> 00:08:32.420
<i>Is that why she hid them?</i>

00:08:38.010 --> 00:08:38.850
<i>LIVE.</i>

00:08:41.180 --> 00:08:43.560
Someone was after material on LIVE.

00:08:44.480 --> 00:08:47.150
If it were stolen...

00:09:01.620 --> 00:09:05.080
When we were young, we both worked
at the same laboratory.

00:09:12.920 --> 00:09:14.130
But that's all.

00:09:14.300 --> 00:09:16.720
I don't know much
about his recent endeavors.

00:09:22.060 --> 00:09:25.270
This was from the council conference
held not too long ago.

00:09:28.770 --> 00:09:31.610
Were you in contact with Mr. Faraday
at all afterwards?

00:09:34.650 --> 00:09:35.610
No.

00:09:54.130 --> 00:09:55.010
Is he...?

00:10:02.810 --> 00:10:04.350
Is he okay?

00:10:05.100 --> 00:10:08.440
We are continuing our search
for Mr. Faraday.

00:10:08.600 --> 00:10:09.850
That's not who I meant.

00:10:12.150 --> 00:10:13.610
I meant Fred's younger brother.

00:10:15.650 --> 00:10:17.110
Geffrey Connor.

00:10:17.610 --> 00:10:20.200
<i>He was also a researcher</i>
<i>for the LIVE Corporation.</i>

00:10:23.030 --> 00:10:23.870
Found him.

00:10:24.700 --> 00:10:27.040
I thought I did a thorough check.

00:10:30.630 --> 00:10:33.130
"Senior Researcher and Executive."

00:10:36.800 --> 00:10:38.380
<i>It's no surprise you didn't know.</i>

00:10:39.470 --> 00:10:43.640
There's only a few people who know
that Fred and Geffrey are brothers.

00:10:45.010 --> 00:10:47.560
And you are one of those few people.

00:10:54.980 --> 00:10:56.320
Connor was with us, too...

00:10:57.990 --> 00:10:59.280
at the same laboratory.

00:11:00.860 --> 00:11:03.450
We were once part of the same team.

00:11:06.700 --> 00:11:08.250
The only thing they had in common

00:11:08.580 --> 00:11:11.080
was being talented scientists.

00:11:12.540 --> 00:11:16.420
Other than that,
they were like oil and water.

00:11:17.920 --> 00:11:18.760
Meaning?

00:11:21.970 --> 00:11:25.970
Fred believed that science
should serve humanity.

00:11:27.060 --> 00:11:30.020
That any research should be conducted
for the people.

00:11:31.100 --> 00:11:32.560
But not Connor.

00:11:34.980 --> 00:11:36.940
He believed science was absolute,

00:11:37.150 --> 00:11:39.740
an entity that transcended mankind.

00:11:41.570 --> 00:11:43.160
<i>His research</i>

00:11:43.570 --> 00:11:45.990
<i>always felt detached from humanity.</i>

00:11:57.050 --> 00:11:58.250
A desire to save.

00:12:00.300 --> 00:12:02.680
I wanted to save someone

00:12:03.260 --> 00:12:04.970
from suffering and sorrow.

00:12:05.890 --> 00:12:07.600
It was a simple wish

00:12:07.930 --> 00:12:10.390
that motivated my research.

00:12:14.190 --> 00:12:15.810
We're veering off topic.

00:12:18.020 --> 00:12:18.860
It's fine.

00:12:20.740 --> 00:12:23.450
I have no idea
where this case may go next.

00:12:24.530 --> 00:12:25.450
There is a chance...

00:12:29.240 --> 00:12:31.370
that you may find yourself in danger.

00:12:34.120 --> 00:12:35.380
Please be on your guard.

00:12:36.580 --> 00:12:37.750
On my guard?

00:12:40.340 --> 00:12:42.260
Thank you for your warning.

00:12:51.980 --> 00:12:53.020
Come in.

00:12:54.060 --> 00:12:55.270
It's time.

00:13:05.280 --> 00:13:07.490
Thank you for taking the time to see me.

00:13:08.490 --> 00:13:10.740
I am happy to cooperate.

00:13:16.960 --> 00:13:20.250
Would you mind
if I asked you one question?

00:13:24.760 --> 00:13:27.720
Do you think it's possible
in the real world...

00:13:28.930 --> 00:13:32.810
for a person to suddenly undergo
rapid aging?

00:13:41.230 --> 00:13:42.780
After undergoing the aging...

00:13:44.110 --> 00:13:45.530
what happens to them?

00:13:46.490 --> 00:13:47.320
They die.

00:13:56.040 --> 00:13:57.370
That's very interesting.

00:13:59.920 --> 00:14:01.000
Thank you very much.

00:14:17.980 --> 00:14:20.190
<i>James, you're going to go?</i>

00:14:21.400 --> 00:14:23.320
Yeah, do you know where it is?

00:14:24.570 --> 00:14:25.530
Connor's residence?

00:14:26.150 --> 00:14:26.990
<i>That's right.</i>

00:14:27.240 --> 00:14:30.620
I have a better chance of meeting him
there at this hour.

00:14:43.460 --> 00:14:44.300
Just sent it over.

00:14:48.510 --> 00:14:49.340
Okay.

00:14:53.640 --> 00:14:54.510
<i>James.</i>

00:14:54.930 --> 00:14:57.980
I'm sharing the information
we learned from Anna with Sarah.

00:15:05.440 --> 00:15:06.940
I was just about to ask you to.

00:15:38.140 --> 00:15:40.520
What do you want to see old footage for?

00:15:42.100 --> 00:15:44.900
I dropped a scarf
that's really important to me.

00:15:45.520 --> 00:15:47.400
It was a gift from my boyfriend.

00:16:14.010 --> 00:16:15.050
That's Monica's room.

00:16:31.570 --> 00:16:32.650
I knew it.

00:16:54.800 --> 00:16:55.640
Monica.

00:17:07.480 --> 00:17:08.480
Whoa, there.

00:17:09.440 --> 00:17:10.320
Robert!

00:17:11.650 --> 00:17:13.240
Please don't shoot me.

00:17:17.990 --> 00:17:19.200
You came back.

00:17:29.790 --> 00:17:31.460
Now it feels like I'm back.

00:17:33.630 --> 00:17:35.010
How was your business trip?

00:17:35.720 --> 00:17:36.840
Boring.

00:17:37.680 --> 00:17:39.720
Just a bunch of sour-looking executives.

00:17:40.720 --> 00:17:42.850
No time to even ogle pretty girls.

00:17:55.070 --> 00:17:55.900
To be honest,

00:17:57.200 --> 00:17:59.030
I wanted to come back right away.

00:18:08.370 --> 00:18:09.380
To Monica.

00:18:16.220 --> 00:18:17.130
We...

00:18:18.300 --> 00:18:20.010
lost a great ally.

00:18:28.020 --> 00:18:31.520
You had a pretty long history with Monica.

00:18:33.110 --> 00:18:34.570
Since we were students.

00:18:36.070 --> 00:18:39.450
Monica really took you under her wing.

00:18:47.040 --> 00:18:49.120
She always had a strong sense of justice.

00:18:51.500 --> 00:18:54.300
I've known her since our lawyering days.

00:18:55.760 --> 00:18:57.590
-What?
-Oh, right.

00:18:58.130 --> 00:19:00.470
You only worked with her as a prosecutor.

00:19:10.480 --> 00:19:11.310
What's wrong?

00:19:12.190 --> 00:19:14.610
Oh, nothing...

00:19:15.320 --> 00:19:16.150
I...

00:19:17.780 --> 00:19:18.610
About Monica--

00:19:20.150 --> 00:19:22.030
-I'm sorry.
-It's okay.

00:19:25.790 --> 00:19:26.740
Is it an emergency?

00:19:27.580 --> 00:19:28.410
No.

00:19:31.580 --> 00:19:34.840
It's my mother. We were supposed to make
Christmas plans.

00:19:36.250 --> 00:19:37.460
Isn't it early for that?

00:19:38.460 --> 00:19:39.840
-So?
-What?

00:19:40.590 --> 00:19:42.050
Weren't you saying something?

00:19:43.050 --> 00:19:44.890
It wasn't important.

00:19:47.100 --> 00:19:49.430
Well, I'm always here if you need to talk.

00:19:53.400 --> 00:19:54.230
Hey...

00:19:55.940 --> 00:19:59.070
I want to thank you for your concern.

00:20:01.860 --> 00:20:05.490
It's the least I can do for being a boss
who's never around.

00:20:07.740 --> 00:20:09.500
That's certainly true.

00:20:12.960 --> 00:20:14.250
What would you like next?

00:20:15.290 --> 00:20:16.130
Let's see.

00:20:18.000 --> 00:20:19.460
I'll have an advocaat.

00:20:20.670 --> 00:20:21.510
What about you?

00:20:22.720 --> 00:20:23.760
A gin and tonic.

00:20:26.180 --> 00:20:28.010
I suppose you being here

00:20:28.510 --> 00:20:30.350
means I have no time to waste.

00:20:40.740 --> 00:20:42.530
That leaves one last thing.

00:20:47.530 --> 00:20:48.740
It's Steven, isn't it?

00:20:49.120 --> 00:20:50.160
Go ahead and answer.

00:20:51.870 --> 00:20:54.330
Give him my regards.

00:21:21.530 --> 00:21:25.740
You make a distinction between people
who can be sacrificed,

00:21:25.860 --> 00:21:27.110
and those who cannot.

00:21:30.030 --> 00:21:33.950
And I appreciate that quality about you.

00:21:37.880 --> 00:21:39.040
I have a favor to ask.

00:21:46.300 --> 00:21:49.390
I'd like you to help someone...

00:21:54.350 --> 00:21:56.060
I'm not willing to sacrifice.

00:22:18.870 --> 00:22:19.920
What's this?

00:22:20.580 --> 00:22:22.170
Steven's orders, I would guess.

00:22:37.180 --> 00:22:39.770
You won't need to worry about Fred.

00:22:41.520 --> 00:22:42.520
What do you mean?

00:24:19.450 --> 00:24:21.960
Subtitle translation by Zensho Yamamoto
